  "The painting is the page (road/page): its frame, DEEDS and its rules, CLOSE. Its tabs and its whole map window are cleared to the panel; CLAIM is lifted so its own crop can be dimmed.",
  "DEEDS / VICTORY ROAD are a TabStrip over the painted row (x 68-870, standing on y 211), in the Deeds' painting's order (road.png had them the other way round): the two pages are one page under two tabs, and DEEDS gives this page's place to the Deeds.",
  "The window is the three road maps stacked in one scroll (road): map_3 (castle) at the top, map_1 (fields) at the foot, each lying 60 rows over the one under it so their mists meet. 776 wide, 1:1: the maps are a `map` kind, and the window is narrowed to them (the painting's was 855) and framed with the painting's reward-box rim.",
  "The fifteen milestones stand on the painted road's centreline, measured on the maps (every row's run of road colour, tracked and smoothed), at even steps along the road that keep each shield off the gate and the two bridges; each carries its reward box on the side the road bends away from.",
  "One stretch band down the window's middle: on 941x2040 the window, its frame and the scroll grow."
